{"t_ms": 746875, "conversation_id": "conv_sentence_end_s0_039", "turn_id": 1, "actor": "system", "event_type": "retrieval_result", "payload": {"passages": ["Yoga & Meditation Sessions\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nComplimentary yoga and meditation sessions are conducted every morning from 6:30 AM to 7:30 AM in the Wellness Studio. Certified instructors guide participants through beginner-friendly exercises focused on relaxation, flexibility, and mindfulness. Prior registration at the Front Desk is recommended due to limited seating.", "Outdoor Sports Activities\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nThe hotel offers outdoor recreational facilities including badminton, basketball, and jogging tracks. Sports equipment can be borrowed from the Recreation Desk during operating hours. Guests are encouraged to wear suitable sports attire and follow all posted safety instructions while using these facilities.", "# corpus/ \u2014 Hotel Documents\n\n**Owner: Lakshya**\n\n## What this folder is\n\nThe hotel's documents live here: the knowledge the assistant answers from. About 60 short \ndocuments covering things like pool and gym hours, check-in and check-out rules, menus, and \npolicies.\n\n## How to fill it\n\nSee the full instructions in `retrieval/README.md` (Step 1). In short:\n- Write ~60 short documents, one topic per file, as `.txt` or `.md`.\n- Make them realistic and varied.\n- Deliberately plant a few contradictions (e.g. one doc says the pool closes at 10 PM, \n  another says 9 PM) and keep a note of which ones, for a later experiment.\n\nThe index-building script reads every file in this folder, so anything you put here becomes \npart of the searchable knowledge.\n"], "scores": [0.6494591236114502, 0.8647435903549194, 0.8940985202789307], "timing_policy": "sentence_end", "timing_trigger": "sentence_end", "user_end_known_at_finish": true, "launch_offset_ms_vs_user_end": 1307, "overlap_with_speech_ms": 0, "forecast_invalidated": false}}
